# Testing LLM Standards

- Add tests only when they validate meaningful application behavior or materially reduce regression risk.
- Prefer tests that cover user-visible or workflow-critical functionality over tests that restate implementation details.
- Avoid tests written only for coverage, symmetry, or habit.
- Favor a small number of high-value tests over many brittle micro-tests.
- Test deterministic behavior, provenance, manifests, retrieval quality, and core CLI or API flows when those behaviors matter to trust.
- Do not lock tests to incidental implementation details such as private helper structure, temporary formatting, or internal call order unless that detail is part of the contract.
